# Vim profile, focus in the file tree (Ctrl-H from the editor, NvChad's
# move into nvim-tree): `:` opens the command line as it does from any
# window, so `:e b.txt<CR>` opens b.txt — and its letters never reach the
# tree's single-key verbs (`x` would cut the row, `d` delete it).
write a.txt "hi\n"
write b.txt "bee\n"
write c.txt "sea\n"
open a.txt
command editor.use_vim
type ":e c.txt\n"
expect pane c.txt
key ctrl+h
expect status contains "\"focus\":\"tree\""
type ":e b.txt\n"
expect pane b.txt
expect screen lacks "cut "
